{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016QadnSsNtkEhcuPUoeDNVw","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Ishihara 1985 \"thickness of liquefiable soil\" surface manifestation criterion sand layer original paper DOI\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Moving towards an improved index for assessing liquefaction hazard: Lessons from historical data - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0038080615000827\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Liquefaction-Induced Ground-Surface Disruption\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/248877804_Liquefaction-Induced_Ground-Surface_Disruption\"},{\"title\":\"LIQUEFACTION-INDUCED GROUND-SURFACE DISRUPTION. TECHNICAL NOTE - TRID\",\"url\":\"https://trid.trb.org/view/451532\"},{\"title\":\"Technical Note 2 – Surface manifestation of liquefaction | GeoAdvanced\",\"url\":\"https://geoadvanced.com/support/tech-notes/surface-manifestation/\"},{\"title\":\"Liquefaction-Induced Ground-Surface Disruption | Journal of Geotechnical Engineering | Vol 121, No 11\",\"url\":\"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/10.1061/(ASCE)0733-9410(1995)121:11(805)\"},{\"title\":\"Evaluation and updating of Ishihara’s (1985) model for liquefaction surface expression, with insights from machine and deep learning - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0038080622000397\"},{\"title\":\"Nationalacademies\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalacademies.org/read/23474/chapter/9\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Limitations of Surface Liquefaction Manifestation Severity Index Models Used in Conjunction with Simplified Stress-Based Triggering Models\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/357376177_Limitations_of_Surface_Liquefaction_Manifestation_Severity_Index_Models_Used_in_Conjunction_with_Simplified_Stress-Based_Triggering_Models\"},{\"title\":\"Evaluation and updating of Ishihara’s (1985) model for liquefaction surface expression, with insights from machine and deep learning | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/359814973_Evaluation_and_updating_of_Ishihara's_1985_model_for_liquefaction_surface_expression_with_insights_from_machine_and_deep_learning\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Investigating the effect of the thickness of the surficial non-liquefiable layer to the surface manifestation of liquefaction-induced failures\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/30047297/Investigating_the_effect_of_the_thickness_of_the_surficial_non_liquefiable_layer_to_the_surface_manifestation_of_liquefaction_induced_failures\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about Ishihara's 1985 work on the thickness of liquefiable soil and surface manifestation criteria. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Original Paper Citation\n\nThe original paper is: Ishihara, K. (1985). \"Stability of natural deposits during earthquakes.\" Proc., 11th Int. Conf. on Soil Mech. and Found. Engrg., Vol. 1, A. A. Balkema, Rotterdam, The Netherlands, 321–376.\n\n## Surface Manifestation Criterion\n\nIshihara plotted observations of liquefaction surface effects using the thicknesses of the non-liquefied capping layer, H1, and the liquefied strata, H2, and proposed boundary curves for predicting liquefaction manifestation as a function of H1, H2, and peak ground acceleration (PGA).\n\nThe boundary curves were developed by Ishihara (1985) using a combination of field performance data from the 1976 Tangshan, China, earthquake, the May 26, 1983 M 7.3 Nihonkai-Chubu (Sea of Japan) earthquake, and professional judgment.\n\n## DOI\n\nUnfortunately, the search results do not contain a DOI (Digital Object Identifier) for this 1985 conference paper. Conference proceedings from that era typically do not have DOIs assigned. You may need to consult the 11th International Conference on Soil Mechanics and Foundation Engineering proceedings directly or check specialized geotechnical engineering databases for any DOI that may have been retroactively assigned.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011wm6d9hWxbGBCfH6BoLdbY","session_id":"2e84c092-3450-428f-a602-fb47a8d85d56","uuid":"fed37626-88f3-4905-b5c6-6c829f3c4082","timestamp":"2026-03-29T20:02:48.553Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JEKPDY5huANTw8tbXU5aqX","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Dobry Ladd 1980 cyclic strain pore pressure threshold shear strain liquefaction prediction NBS 1982 full citation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Chapter: 5 Alternative Approaches to Liquefaction ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalacademies.org/read/23474/chapter/7\"},{\"title\":\"Google Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?title=Prediction+of+pore+water+pressure+buildup+and+liquefaction+of+sands+during+earthquakes+by+the+cyclic+strain+method&amp=&author=R.+Dobry&amp=&author=R.+S.+Ladd&amp=&author=F.+Y.+Yokel&amp=&author=R.+M.+Chung&amp=&author=D.+Powell&amp=&publication_year=1982&amp=&pages=138&amp=&doi=10.6028/NBS.BSS.138\"},{\"title\":\"NEHRP Clearing House\",\"url\":\"https://nehrpsearch.nist.gov/article/PB83-111617/XAB\"},{\"title\":\"1 Cyclic Shear Strain Needed for Liquefaction Triggering and\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Ricardo-Dobry/publication/279239866_Cyclic_Shear_Strain_Needed_for_Liquefaction_Triggering_and_Assessment_of_Overburden_Pressure_Factor_Ks/links/559a8f5d08ae5d8f3937dbc3/Cyclic-Shear-Strain-Needed-for-Liquefaction-Triggering-and-Assessment-of-Overburden-Pressure-Factor-Ks.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Frontiers | Cyclic threshold shear strain for pore water pressure generation and stiffness degradation in marine clays at Yangtze estuary\",\"url\":\"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/marine-science/articles/10.3389/fmars.2023.1184225/full\"},{\"title\":\"Full article: Strain-based assessment of liquefaction and seismic settlement of saturated sand\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/23311916.2019.1573788\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Strain energy base evaluation of liquefaction and residual pore water pressure in sands using cyclic torsional shear experiments\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/2099019/Strain_energy_base_evaluation_of_liquefaction_and_residual_pore_water_pressure_in_sands_using_cyclic_torsional_shear_experiments\"},{\"title\":\"An experimental database for the development, calibration and verification of constitutive models for sand with focus to cyclic loading: part II—tests with strain cycles and combined loading | Acta Geotechnica | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11440-015-0412-x\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Cyclic Shear Strain Needed for Liquefaction Triggering and Assessment of Overburden Pressure Factor Kσ\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/279239866_Cyclic_Shear_Strain_Needed_for_Liquefaction_Triggering_and_Assessment_of_Overburden_Pressure_Factor_Ks\"},{\"title\":\"Estimation of Excess Pore Pressure Generation and Nonlinear Site Response of Liquefied Areas | IntechOpen\",\"url\":\"https://www.intechopen.com/chapters/68777\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found the full citation for the publication you're looking for:\n\nDobry, R., Ladd, R. S., Yokel, F. Y., Chung, R. M., & Powell, D. (1982). Prediction of pore water pressure buildup and liquefaction of sands during earthquakes by the cyclic strain method. National Bureau of Standards Building Science Series, 138, 150.\n\nThe work is also referenced as Dobry R, Ladd RS, Yokel FY, Chung RM, Powell D. Prediction of Pore Water Pressure Buildup and Liquefaction of Sands during Earthquakes by the Cyclic Strain Method, NBS Building Science Series 138. Gaithersburg, Maryland: National Bureau of Standards; 1982.\n\nThe DOI for this publication is: 10.6028/NBS.BSS.138\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011wm6d9hWxbGBCfH6BoLdbY","session_id":"2e84c092-3450-428f-a602-fb47a8d85d56","uuid":"64d9b812-dfc8-46e8-af41-9bc77640000c","timestamp":"2026-03-29T20:02:49.280Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GeZQGkt385MEXaC8J7ccHz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"improved notion\" \"strain ratio\" equivalent linear site response 2024 Bulletin Earthquake Engineering DOI 10.1007\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"An improved notion for the computation of strain ratio in equivalent linear site response | Bulletin of Earthquake Engineering\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10518-024-02061-1\"},{\"title\":\"Geotechnical Earthquake Engineering\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/298035737_Geotechnical_Earthquake_Engineering\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction to the Special Section on Advances in Site Response Estimation | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/353063029_Introduction_to_the_Special_Section_on_Advances_in_Site_Response_Estimation\"}]\n\nI found the article you're looking for! \n\nThe paper \"An improved notion for the computation of strain ratio in equivalent linear site response\" by Sinha, R. was published in Bulletin of Earthquake Engineering 23, 53–82 (2025), with DOI 10.1007/s10518-024-02061-1.\n\nThe article was published on December 10, 2024. \n\nThe research addresses a significant limitation in equivalent linear site response analysis. The study notes that surface ground motion characteristics predicted employing EQLSRA are often overdamped, especially at high frequencies, with the algorithm used for obtaining the Equivalent Shear Strain being identified as a primary reason for unsatisfactory performance.\n\nThe proposed method takes into account the frequency content and intensity in the induced seismic strain waveform for the determination of strain ratio. Testing the modified EQLSRA with 15 KiK-net stations and 110 ground motions found that the average absolute error in surface Peak Horizontal Acceleration predicted reduces by approximately 54% compared to traditional EQLSRA.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011wm6d9hWxbGBCfH6BoLdbY","session_id":"2e84c092-3450-428f-a602-fb47a8d85d56","uuid":"1a8abfc0-fbef-4edb-93e8-8bc97a514bae","timestamp":"2026-03-29T20:02:49.323Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0193fSyFqASzLXmMq5w5ikSy","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Seed Booker 1977 stabilization fine cohesionless soils cyclic loading pore pressure DOI ASCE journal geotechnical\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"(PDF) An Energy-Based Excess Pore Pressure Generation Model for Cohesionless Soils\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/265564025_An_Energy-Based_Excess_Pore_Pressure_Generation_Model_for_Cohesionless_Soils\"},{\"title\":\"Pore Pressure Generation of Gravelly Soils in Constant Volume Cyclic Simple Shear | Journal of Geotechnical and Geoenvironmental Engineering | Vol 149, No 2\",\"url\":\"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/abs/10.1061/(ASCE)GT.1943-5606.0002928\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Pore Pressure Generation Models for Sands and Silty Soils Subjected to Cyclic Loading\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/245294607_Pore_Pressure_Generation_Models_for_Sands_and_Silty_Soils_Subjected_to_Cyclic_Loading\"},{\"title\":\"Plasticity Model for Sand under Small and Large Cyclic Strains | Journal of Geotechnical and Geoenvironmental Engineering | Vol 127, No 11\",\"url\":\"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/10.1061/(ASCE)1090-0241(2001)127:11(973)\"},{\"title\":\"Undrained Strength Characteristics of Cohesionless Soils | Journal of the Soil Mechanics and Foundations Division | Vol 93, No 6\",\"url\":\"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/10.1061/JSFEAQ.0001059\"},{\"title\":\"In Situ Pore-Pressure Generation Behavior of Liquefiable Sand | Journal of Geotechnical and Geoenvironmental Engineering | Vol 133, No 8\",\"url\":\"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/10.1061/(ASCE)1090-0241(2007)133:8(921)\"},{\"title\":\"Cyclic Large Strain and Induced Pore Pressure Models for Saturated Clean Sands | Journal of Geotechnical and Geoenvironmental Engineering | Vol 138, No 3\",\"url\":\"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/abs/10.1061/(ASCE)GT.1943-5606.0000631\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Analysis of Pore Pressure Generation and Dissipation in Cohesionless Materials During Seismic Loading\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/237291511_Analysis_of_Pore_Pressure_Generation_and_Dissipation_in_Cohesionless_Materials_During_Seismic_Loading\"},{\"title\":\"Moduli and Damping Factors for Dynamic Analyses of Cohesionless Soils | Journal of Geotechnical Engineering | Vol 112, No 11\",\"url\":\"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/abs/10.1061/(ASCE)0733-9410(1986)112:11(1016)\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Pore Pressure Generation Models for Sands and Silty Soils Subjected to Cyclic Loading\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/16038741/Pore_Pressure_Generation_Models_for_Sands_and_Silty_Soils_Subjected_to_Cyclic_Loading\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the Seed and Booker 1977 publication you're looking for:\n\nSeed, H.B. & Booker, J.R. 1977 published \"Stabilization of Potentially Liquefiable Sand Deposits Using Gravel Drain Systems\" in the ASCE Journal of the Geotechnical Engineering Division 103(GT7): 757- (the full page range ends at 768 based on other search results).\n\nThis paper, which appears multiple times in the references of various geotechnical research studies, addresses the stabilization of potentially liquefiable sand deposits—cohesionless soils—under cyclic loading conditions and relates to pore pressure development. The publication is located in a recognized ASCE journal focused on geotechnical engineering.\n\nThe search results indicate this is a seminal work that has been widely cited in subsequent research on pore pressure generation in cohesionless soils subjected to cyclic loading, though the specific DOI was not returned in these search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011wm6d9hWxbGBCfH6BoLdbY","session_id":"2e84c092-3450-428f-a602-fb47a8d85d56","uuid":"2facf7f8-2499-4f66-b86d-89c98fd23b0f","timestamp":"2026-03-29T20:02:50.756Z"}
