{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015X96ugSeEUVBv1szQhmc4R","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Boulanger Ziotopoulou 2015 2017 PM4Sand version 3 report UCD CGM DOI\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"PM4Sand Files | PM4Sand\",\"url\":\"https://pm4sand.engr.ucdavis.edu/pm4sand-files\"},{\"title\":\"CENTER FOR GEOTECHNICAL MODELING REPORT NO. UCD/CGM-15/01 PM4SAND (VERSION 3):\",\"url\":\"https://faculty.engineering.ucdavis.edu/boulanger/wp-content/uploads/sites/71/2014/09/Boulanger_Ziotopoulou_PM4Sand_Model_CGM-15-01_2015.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"PM4Sand References | PM4Sand\",\"url\":\"https://pm4sand.engr.ucdavis.edu/pm4sand-references\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) PM4Sand Version 3: A Sand Plasticity Model for Earthquake Engineering Applications\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/273694951_PM4Sand_Version_3_A_Sand_Plasticity_Model_for_Earthquake_Engineering_Applications\"},{\"title\":\"Earthquake Engineering with Uncertainty Quantification Application (EE-UQ) — Earthquake Engineering with Uncertainty Quantification documentation\",\"url\":\"https://nheri-simcenter.github.io/EE-UQ-Documentation/\"},{\"title\":\"Google Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?title=PM4Sand+(version+3.1):+A+sand+plasticity+model+for+earthquake+engineering+applications.&amp=&author=R.+W.+Boulanger&amp=&author=K.+Ziotopoulou&amp=&publication_year=2017\"},{\"title\":\"Performance Based Engineering Application — Performance Based Engineering Application documentation\",\"url\":\"https://nheri-simcenter.github.io/PBE-Documentation/\"},{\"title\":\"PM4SAND (VERSION 3.3): A SAND PLASTICITY MODEL ...\",\"url\":\"https://itasca-software.s3.amazonaws.com/udm-library/Boulanger_Ziotopoulou_PM4Sand_v3.3_CGM-23-01.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Numerical modelling of the effect of horizontal drains in centrifuge tests on soil-structure interaction in liquefiable soils | Bulletin of Earthquake Engineering | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10518-021-01084-2\"},{\"title\":\"CENTER FOR GEOTECHNICAL MODELING REPORT NO. UCD/CGM-18/01 PM4SILT (VERSION 1):\",\"url\":\"https://itasca-software.s3.amazonaws.com/udm-library/Boulanger_Ziotopoulou_PM4Silt_Model_CGM-18-01_2018.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the Boulanger and Ziotopoulou PM4Sand reports from the specified years and report number:\n\n## PM4Sand Version 3 (2015)\n\nBoulanger, R. W., and Ziotopoulou, K. (2015). \"PM4Sand (Version 3): A sand plasticity model for earthquake engineering applications.\" Report No. UCD/CGM-15/01, Center for Geotechnical Modeling, Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering, University of California, Davis, CA, March, 112 pp.\n\n## PM4Sand Version 3.1 (2017)\n\nBoulanger, R. W., and Ziotopoulou, K. (2017). \"PM4Sand (Version 3.1): A sand plasticity model for earthquake engineering applications.\" Report No. UCD/CGM-17/01, Center for Geotechnical Modeling, Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering, University of California, Davis, CA, March, 114 pp.\n\nThe 2015 report (UCD/CGM-15/01) is available at the official PM4Sand website. However, the search results do not include specific DOI information for these reports. These appear to be technical reports rather than journal articles, which typically use DOIs. If you need the DOI, it would be best to check the University of California Davis library system or contact the Center for Geotechnical Modeling directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011wm6d9hWxbGBCfH6BoLdbY","session_id":"2e84c092-3450-428f-a602-fb47a8d85d56","uuid":"3ee12a7d-61ac-462b-ab07-cc6d6e667b37","timestamp":"2026-03-29T20:03:13.075Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qu5zkEvRcYNiuVvWDr2Gh1","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Carlton Tokimatsu 2016 \"comparison equivalent linear nonlinear site response\" \"maximum shear strain\" DOI Earthquake Spectra 10.1193\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Comparison of Equivalent Linear and Nonlinear Site Response Analysis Results and Model to Estimate Maximum Shear Strain - Brian Carlton, Kohji Tokimatsu, 2016\",\"url\":\"https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/abs/10.1193/021215EQS029MR1\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Comparison of Equivalent Linear and Nonlinear Site Response Analysis Results and Model to Estimate Maximum Shear Strain\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/285619629_Comparison_of_Equivalent_Linear_and_Nonlinear_Site_Response_Analysis_Results_and_Model_to_Estimate_Maximum_Shear_Strain\"},{\"title\":\"Comparison of Equivalent Linear and Nonlinear Site Response Analysis Results and Model to Estimate Maximum Shear Strain\",\"url\":\"https://chooser.crossref.org/?doi=10.1193/021215EQS029MR1\"},{\"title\":\"Comparison of Equivalent Linear and Nonlinear Site Response Analysis Results and Model to Estimate Maximum Shear Strain | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/306268835_Comparison_of_Equivalent_Linear_and_Nonlinear_Site_Response_Analysis_Results_and_Model_to_Estimate_Maximum_Shear_Strain\"},{\"title\":\"Divergence Between Nonlinear and Equivalent-Linear 1D Site Response Analyses for Different V S Realizations of Typical Clay Sites - Pure and Applied Geophysics\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00024-017-1586-y?error=cookies_not_supported&code=fe0edde9-06ce-4abe-8c5d-9d01aab7a789\"},{\"title\":\"Evaluation of site effects on ground motions based on equivalent linear site response analysis and liquefaction potential in Chennai, south India | Journal of Seismology | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10950-018-9751-z\"},{\"title\":\"Effect of site specific soil characteristics on the nonlinear ground response analysis and comparison of the results with equivalent linear analysis - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0926985123003282\"},{\"title\":\"Comparison of Equivalent Linear and Non Linear Methods ...\",\"url\":\"https://media.neliti.com/media/publications/127438-comparison-of-equivalent-linear-and-non-da35c8e8.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"A simulation-based nonlinear site amplification model for ground-motion prediction equations in Japan | Earthquake Engineering and Engineering Vibration\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11803-021-2058-z\"},{\"title\":\"In situ assessment of soil dynamic parameters for characterizing nonlinear seismic site response using KiK-net vertical array data | Bulletin of Earthquake Engineering\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10518-018-00539-3\"}]\n\nI found the article you're looking for! Here are the search results:\n\n## Publication Details\n\nThe article \"Comparison of Equivalent Linear and Nonlinear Site Response Analysis Results and Model to Estimate Maximum Shear Strain\" by Brian Carlton and Kohji Tokimatsu was published in Earthquake Spectra in August 2016 with DOI 10.1193/021215eqs029mr1.\n\n## Key Findings\n\nThe authors compared equivalent linear analysis (ELA) and nonlinear site response analysis (NLA) and found that differences between peak ground acceleration (PGA), peak ground velocity (PGV), Arias intensity (Ia), significant duration (D5–75), and response spectrum for periods between 0.025 s and 2 s predicted by each method are non-negligible for maximum shear strain values predicted by ELA (γmax,ELA) greater than 0.04% to 1.0%.\n\nAs γmax,ELA increases, ELA in general predict smaller shear strain and D5–75 values, and larger PGA, PGV, Ia, mean period, and response spectral values for periods less than 0.1 s and periods near the natural site period than NLA.\n\nTo help researchers and practitioners decide when to use ELA and/or NLA, the authors developed a model to estimate γmax,ELA before conducting a site response analysis.\n\nThe article is available through multiple sources including SAGE Publications and GeoScience World.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011wm6d9hWxbGBCfH6BoLdbY","session_id":"2e84c092-3450-428f-a602-fb47a8d85d56","uuid":"c977fb49-3ca8-423d-a644-53a1942f08cb","timestamp":"2026-03-29T20:03:13.709Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DEh7y5Bh1Ar3quovP94ahu","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Seismic Site Response Analysis Pore Water Pressure Generation Guidelines National Academies 2023 DOI\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Seismic Site Response Analysis with Pore Water Pressure Generation: Guidelines | The National Academies Press\",\"url\":\"https://nap.nationalacademies.org/catalog/27536/seismic-site-response-analysis-with-pore-water-pressure-generation-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Chapter 4 - Basis for Development of Guidelines | Seismic Site Response Analysis with Pore Water Pressure Generation: Guidelines | The National Academies Press\",\"url\":\"https://nap.nationalacademies.org/read/27536/chapter/5\"},{\"title\":\"Chapter 2 - Site Response Analysis Overview | Seismic Site Response Analysis with Pore Water Pressure Generation: Guidelines | The National Academies Press\",\"url\":\"https://nap.nationalacademies.org/read/27536/chapter/3\"},{\"title\":\"Abbreviations, Acronyms, Initialisms, and Symbols | Seismic Site Response Analysis with Pore Water Pressure Generation: Guidelines | The National Academies Press\",\"url\":\"https://nap.nationalacademies.org/read/27536/chapter/12\"},{\"title\":\"Chapter 3 - Site Response Analysis Theoretical Background | Seismic Site Response Analysis with Pore Water Pressure Generation: Guidelines | The National Academies Press\",\"url\":\"https://nap.nationalacademies.org/read/27536/chapter/4\"},{\"title\":\"Endnotes | Seismic Site Response Analysis with Pore ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalacademies.org/read/27536/chapter/14\"},{\"title\":\"Trb\",\"url\":\"https://apps.trb.org/cmsfeed/TRBNetProjectDisplay.asp?ProjectID=4366\"},{\"title\":\"Chapter 1 - Introduction | Seismic Site Response Analysis with Pore Water Pressure Generation: Guidelines | The National Academies Press\",\"url\":\"https://nap.nationalacademies.org/read/27536/chapter/2\"},{\"title\":\"References | Seismic Site Response Analysis with Pore Water Pressure Generation: Guidelines | The National Academies Press\",\"url\":\"https://nap.nationalacademies.org/read/27536/chapter/11\"},{\"title\":\"Chapter 6 - Field and Experimental Programs | Seismic Site Response Analysis with Pore Water Pressure Generation: Guidelines | The National Academies Press\",\"url\":\"https://nap.nationalacademies.org/read/27536/chapter/7\"}]\n\n## Search Results\n\nI've successfully found information about the publication you requested. Here are the key details:\n\n**Publication Information:**\n- National Academies of Sciences, Engineering, and Medicine. 2024. Seismic Site Response Analysis with Pore Water Pressure Generation: Guidelines.\n- Washington, DC: The National Academies Press.\n- DOI: https://doi.org/10.17226/27536\n\n**About the Document:**\nNCHRP Research Report 1092: Seismic Site Response Analysis with Pore Water Pressure Generation: Guidelines presents guidelines for the selection and use of methods for 1D nonlinear seismic SRA with excess pore water pressure generation and dissipation. Supplemental to the report is NCHRP Web-Only Document 383: Seismic Site Response Analysis with Pore Water Pressure Generation: Resources for Evaluation.\n\n**Note:** While your query mentioned 2023, the actual publication date is 2024 (though the research was completed in early 2023).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011wm6d9hWxbGBCfH6BoLdbY","session_id":"2e84c092-3450-428f-a602-fb47a8d85d56","uuid":"4b3646e6-19ce-4e36-a779-95be744a9624","timestamp":"2026-03-29T20:03:14.813Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K8fHHfHpZctibiARfFn6Mt","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"van Ballegooy 2014 \"assessment liquefaction-induced land damage\" Christchurch Earthquake Spectra DOI 10.1193\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Assessment of Liquefaction-Induced Land Damage for Residential Christchurch - S. van Ballegooy, P. Malan, V. Lacrosse, M. E. Jacka, M. Cubrinovski, J. D. Bray, T. D. O'Rourke, S. A. Crawford, H. Cowan, 2014\",\"url\":\"https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1193/031813EQS070M\"},{\"title\":\"Assessment of Liquefaction-Induced Land Damage for Residential Christchurch | Earthquake Spectra | GeoScienceWorld\",\"url\":\"https://pubs.geoscienceworld.org/eeri/earthquake-spectra/article/30/1/31/587076/Assessment-of-Liquefaction-Induced-Land-Damage-for\"},{\"title\":\"Full article: Mapping surface liquefaction caused by the September 2010 and February 2011 Canterbury earthquakes: a digital dataset\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/00288306.2016.1182929\"},{\"title\":\"Google Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?title=Assessment+of+liquefaction-induced+land+damage+for+residential+Christchurch&amp=&author=S.+van+Ballegooy&amp=&author=P.+Malan&amp=&author=V.+Lacrosse&amp=&author=M.+E.+Jacka&amp=&author=M.+Cubrinovski&amp=&author=J.+D.+Bray&amp=&author=T.+D.+O%E2%80%99Rourke&amp=&author=S.+A.+Crawford&amp=&author=H.+Cowan&amp=&publication_year=2014&amp=&journal=Earthquake+Spectra&amp=&pages=31-55&amp=&doi=10.1193/031813EQS070M\"},{\"title\":\"Evaluation of Liquefaction Ejecta Case Histories in Christchurch | Proceedings | Vol , No\",\"url\":\"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/10.1061/9780784484043.050\"},{\"title\":\"Figure 14 from Assessment of Liquefaction-Induced Land Damage for Residential Christchurch | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Assessment-of-Liquefaction-Induced-Land-Damage-for-Ballegooy-Malan/d440b49dd2bce062cb33d98c54440c5d044f43c8/figure/15\"},{\"title\":\"Assessment of Liquefaction-Induced Land Damage for Residential Christchurch | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/273663937_Assessment_of_Liquefaction-Induced_Land_Damage_for_Residential_Christchurch\"},{\"title\":\"Limitations of Surface Liquefaction Manifestation Severity Index Models Used in Conjunction with Simplified Stress-Based Triggering Models | Journal of Geotechnical and Geoenvironmental Engineering | Vol 148, No 3\",\"url\":\"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/abs/10.1061/(ASCE)GT.1943-5606.0002725\"},{\"title\":\"Fluvial geomorphic factors affecting liquefaction-induced lateral spreading - Nancy Ingabire Abayo, Ashly Cabas, Ellen Chamberlin, Brina Montoya, 2023\",\"url\":\"https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/87552930231190655\"},{\"title\":\"Comparison of CPT-based simplified liquefaction ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.issmge.org/uploads/publications/89/100/12ANZ_082.pdf\"}]\n\nI found the paper you're looking for! Here are the details:\n\nThe paper \"Assessment of Liquefaction-Induced Land Damage for Residential Christchurch\" was published in Earthquake Spectra, Volume 30, Issue 1, pages 31–55 in 2014. The authors are S. van Ballegooy, P. Malan, V. Lacrosse, M. E. Jacka, M. Cubrinovski, J. D. Bray, T. D. O'Rourke, S. A. Crawford, and H. Cowan.\n\nThe DOI is 10.1193/031813EQS070M.\n\nThe paper describes the land damage assessment process for Christchurch, including the collection and processing of extensive data and observations related to liquefaction, the characterization of liquefaction effects on land performance, and the quantification of losses for insurance compensation purposes.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011wm6d9hWxbGBCfH6BoLdbY","session_id":"2e84c092-3450-428f-a602-fb47a8d85d56","uuid":"44920129-13b4-4607-8f8f-82584335f69a","timestamp":"2026-03-29T