{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KdhDXcARJz1vXH9Hyt4hzs","type":"tool_result","content":"# pyStrata Python Package\n\n**Full Name:** pyStrata\n\n**Author:** arkottke (Allin Cottke)\n\n**Purpose:** This toolkit provides \"tools for modeling wave propagation through layered soil profiles and computing surface ground motion from bedrock input motions.\" It supports both time-series and random vibration theory approaches, with equivalent-linear and frequency-domain methods available.\n\n**Citation & DOI:** The package has a Zenodo DOI for citation purposes: **https://zenodo.org/badge/latestdoi/8959678**\n\nThe repository indicates this is research software with an MIT license, making it suitable for academic and commercial applications."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011wm6d9hWxbGBCfH6BoLdbY","session_id":"2e84c092-3450-428f-a602-fb47a8d85d56","uuid":"66455509-a450-4a40-b3ed-d210773ebaa5","timestamp":"2026-03-29T20:03:40.425Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013QqPnMms3NxyHDshsuL81X","type":"tool_result","content":"# PySeismoSoil Overview\n\n## Authors\nThe library was created by members of the Geoquake Research Group at Caltech: Jian Shi, Domniki Asimaki, Wei Li, and Flora Xia.\n\n## Citation & DOI\nUsers should cite this library using its Zenodo DOI: **10.5281/zenodo.169386936**\n\n## Purpose\nPySeismoSoil is \"a Python library for performing 1D seismic site response analysis.\" It enables researchers and engineers to model how soil layers respond to earthquake ground motion in one-dimensional simulations, drawing on foundational work in geotechnical earthquake engineering and nonlinear soil modeling."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011wm6d9hWxbGBCfH6BoLdbY","session_id":"2e84c092-3450-428f-a602-fb47a8d85d56","uuid":"e3777e9b-4ff5-4fdc-b2e3-902e21a67071","timestamp":"2026-03-29T20:03:40.569Z"}
