{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DXD9RajpcmBFNmBta53xq7","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Olson Mei Hashash 2020 \"nonlinear site response\" pore pressure generation liquefaction triggering JGGE authors full\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Nonlinear Site Response Analysis with Pore-Water Pressure Generation for Liquefaction Triggering Evaluation - Illinois Experts\",\"url\":\"https://experts.illinois.edu/en/publications/nonlinear-site-response-analysis-with-pore-water-pressure-generat/\"},{\"title\":\"Nonlinear Site Response Analysis with Pore-Water Pressure Generation for Liquefaction Triggering Evaluation | Journal of Geotechnical and Geoenvironmental Engineering | Vol 146, No 2\",\"url\":\"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/abs/10.1061/(ASCE)GT.1943-5606.0002191\"},{\"title\":\"Displacement-Based Design of Axially Loaded Piles for Seismic Loading and Liquefaction-Induced Downdrag | Journal of Geotechnical and Geoenvironmental Engineering | Vol 149, No 9\",\"url\":\"https://ascelibrary.org/doi/abs/10.1061/JGGEFK.GTENG-11178\"},{\"title\":\"Non-linear seismic response for liquefaction analysis: pore water pressure and strain ratio approach | Scientific Review Engineering and Environmental Sciences (SREES)\",\"url\":\"https://srees.sggw.edu.pl/article/view/10426\"},{\"title\":\"Nonlinear Site Response Analysis With Pore-Water Pressure Generation For Liquefaction Triggering Evaluation | PDF | Moment Magnitude Scale | Stress (Mechanics)\",\"url\":\"https://www.scribd.com/document/549517730/ASCE-GT-1943-5606-0002191\"},{\"title\":\"Youssef M. A. Hashash | Civil & Environmental Engineering | Illinois\",\"url\":\"https://cee.illinois.edu/directory/profile/hashash\"},{\"title\":\"Nonlinear Site Response Analysis with Pore-Water Pressure Generation for Liquefaction Triggering Evaluation | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/338972983_Nonlinear_Site_Response_Analysis_with_Pore-Water_Pressure_Generation_for_Liquefaction_Triggering_Evaluation\"},{\"title\":\"Site‐specific liquefaction fragility analysis: Cloud, stripe, and incremental approaches - Bullock - 2021 - Earthquake Engineering & Structural Dynamics - Wiley Online Library\",\"url\":\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1002/eqe.3458\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Correlation of excess pore water pressure ratio on flow liquefaction phenomenon in Sibalaya – Central Sulawesi Province\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/374056629_Correlation_of_excess_pore_water_pressure_ratio_on_flow_liquefaction_phenomenon_in_Sibalaya_-_Central_Sulawesi_Province\"},{\"title\":\"Pore pressure generation and liquefaction analysis using nonlinear, effective stress-based site response analysis | IDEALS\",\"url\":\"https://www.ideals.illinois.edu/items/109954\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found the paper you're looking for:\n\nThe authors are Olson, S. M., Mei, X., & Hashash, Y. M. A., and the paper \"Nonlinear Site Response Analysis with Pore-Water Pressure Generation for Liquefaction Triggering Evaluation\" was published in 2020 in the Journal of Geotechnical and Geoenvironmental Engineering, Volume 146, Number 2, Article 04019128.\n\nThe full author names are:\n- Scott M. Olson\n- Xuan Mei\n- Youssef M.A. Hashash\n\nThe publication details show: Scott M. Olson, Ph.D., M.ASCE, Xuan Mei, S.M.ASCE, and Youssef M. A. Hashash, Ph.D., F.ASCE in the Journal of Geotechnical and Geoenvironmental Engineering.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011wm6d9hWxbGBCfH6BoLdbY","session_id":"2e84c092-3450-428f-a602-fb47a8d85d56","uuid":"e7821f6b-dc8d-4904-b2c1-739cf3b4e9f8","timestamp":"2026-03-29T20:03:50.884Z"}
